options that we should have

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.450
in order to have more of

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:11.460
a competitive political marketplace.

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:12.930
- But wouldn't it make it more political

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:15.150
for the people to choose their judges?

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:16.380
- Yes, absolutely.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:17.850
- I'm pretty sure we do vote in the people

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:19.170
that pick the Supreme Court justice.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.003
- You vote for the president.

00:21:20.003 --> 00:21:20.848
- We vote for the president.

00:21:20.848 --> 00:21:22.353
(inaudible crosstalk)

00:21:22.353 --> 00:21:24.450
- Also not necessarily
like jurisprudential

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.256
or like law in particular.

00:21:26.256 --> 00:21:27.120
(dramatic music)

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:30.550
- [Interviewer] I'm hopeful
about my future in this country.

00:21:32.077 --> 00:21:34.410
(footsteps)

00:21:35.873 --> 00:21:37.680
- Here in the United
States we have the ability

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:39.450
and the opportunity to be the best nation

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.190
in the world and live up to all the ideals

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:42.023
that we grew up with
and thought that we had.

00:21:42.023 --> 00:21:44.610
Look at all of us, we're
willing to have a conversation

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.560
whereas years ago we
might not have sat down,

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:48.210
we might have hated each other
for having different types

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:49.043
of beliefs.

00:21:49.043 --> 00:21:51.120
So I really think that shows
the type of growth potential

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.052
that the United States has in particular.

00:21:53.052 --> 00:21:56.207
- I personally think I have a
great future in this country,

00:21:56.207 --> 00:21:59.910
especially being a woman
because I can sit here

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:00.810
and wear what I want,

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:02.790
say what I want and
have just as many rights

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.268
and equal facilities as you
do as in other countries

00:22:05.268 --> 00:22:08.910
that's not awarded to all
women or even all people.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:10.860
And I feel that our country gives us some

00:22:10.860 --> 00:22:12.330
of the most privilege in the world.

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:14.640
- So for me right now,
I live a great life.

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:15.797
I have a house, I have a cat,

00:22:15.797 --> 00:22:18.052
I have two dogs and it's great.

00:22:18.052 --> 00:22:21.930
But I feel like things could
always be better, you know?

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:25.020
And I think that's what
I like about this country

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:26.700
is that we have a government where

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.590
we can actively participate in

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:31.503
and we can make the changes
that we want to see.

00:22:34.710 --> 00:22:38.490
- I think that I am very
scared for my future.

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:43.080
I grew up two hours away from
a Ku Klux Klan headquarters.

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:44.490
If that tells you anything
about where I grew up,

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:47.580
there's probably less
than the amount of fingers

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:50.040
I have on my hands of people
of color in my school.

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:53.250
There was a lot of racial
heat that I got growing up

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:54.870
and it forced me to grow up a lot faster

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:56.250
than I thought that I'd have to.

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:57.840
Cause if you look up Harrison, Arkansas,

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:01.350
it's known as one of the most
racist cities in America.

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:04.200
And you can see if you're on
TikTok and you see we visited

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:05.435
the most racist city in America,

00:23:05.435 --> 00:23:07.380
that's gonna be Harrison, Arkansas.

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:08.310
My mother is white.

00:23:08.310 --> 00:23:11.100
But whenever my mom would
drive through Harrison when we

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:12.120
were going somewhere,

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:14.710
she would put a blanket
over my crib while we were

00:23:15.646 --> 00:23:18.480
in that city just because
she felt unsafe for me.

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:21.035
And whenever I hosted the
Black Lives Matter protest,

00:23:21.035 --> 00:23:24.300
a lot of members from that
Ku Klux Klan organization

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:26.490
in Harrison were making groups saying

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:28.907
that they were gonna come up
and harass us and harm us.

00:23:28.907 --> 00:23:32.070
And it's a very scary thing
because you read about

00:23:32.070 --> 00:23:34.350
the Ku Klux Klan in history books.

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:37.980
It's a very different thing to
hear them personally tweeting

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:39.720
out to you that they're gonna come

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:41.190
and that they're gonna harm you.

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:42.840
As much as our country is growing,

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:44.700
I'm also not gonna invalidate
the fact that there is

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:48.270
a lot of issues that are
still stemmed very deep

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:50.160
in a lot of people's brains that are still

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:53.010
being acted out upon and
causing me to feel uncomfortable

00:23:53.010 --> 00:23:54.360
to live in my country.

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:55.890
- As a black woman.

00:23:55.890 --> 00:23:58.860
I just feel like being
anywhere in the world,

00:23:58.860 --> 00:24:00.330
it's not just America.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:02.550
There will always be somebody
who does not like a person

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:04.230
of color and there will
always be someone who wants

00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:05.400
to assault a woman.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:07.560
We are making progress,
but in the same way

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.240
we can always go backwards.

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:11.640
In Detroit, I just was not happy.

00:24:11.640 --> 00:24:13.980
Being around white kids at school,

00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.254
I don't think they,

00:24:15.254 --> 00:24:19.170
I think they are taught to
believe that black people

00:24:19.170 --> 00:24:22.650
are maybe lower than them
and even if it's not taught,

00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:26.850
it's something ingrained just in society.

00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:28.770
- As someone who is not, you know,

00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:32.550
quite as dark as you but lives
kind of a similar lifestyle.

00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:35.550
I'm trying to say is that
I understand, I really do.

00:24:35.550 --> 00:24:37.860
It's still a thing that
can be stronger than ever,

00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:39.960
especially with the
benefit of social media.

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:42.090
I think it's something that
we need to grow past if we're

00:24:42.090 --> 00:24:43.950
going to make the world
better for our children.

00:24:43.950 --> 00:24:45.630
But I think we're also right here,

00:24:45.630 --> 00:24:47.970
which is a very diverse
group in and of itself.

00:24:47.970 --> 00:24:49.800
But I think we're gonna
be one of the least racist

00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:51.840
generations ever, which
kind of goes without saying.

00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:54.300
And I think this will be the
century that that is just

00:24:54.300 --> 00:24:56.400
completely eradicated,
at least systemically.

00:24:56.400 --> 00:24:57.960
- Well I hope you're
right and it obviously

00:24:57.960 --> 00:24:59.640
is a privilege to live
in the United States,

00:24:59.640 --> 00:25:01.950
but I think we're going
down a very dangerous path.

00:25:01.950 --> 00:25:03.750
Freedom of speech is under
attack in this country.

00:25:03.750 --> 00:25:05.580
Freedom of thought is under attack.

00:25:05.580 --> 00:25:07.860
The standard of living has
decreased dramatically.

00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:09.146
People are, are just,

00:25:09.146 --> 00:25:11.970
aren't doing better today
than they were 10 years ago

00:25:11.970 --> 00:25:12.990
or 20 years ago.

00:25:12.990 --> 00:25:14.340
- What do you mean we're
doing worse off now?

00:25:14.340 --> 00:25:16.547
Like what are you looking at in terms

00:25:16.547 --> 00:25:17.520
of how did you determine whether

00:25:17.520 --> 00:25:19.020
or not we're doing worse off?

00:25:19.020 --> 00:25:20.160
- Well there's so many things to look at.

00:25:20.160 --> 00:25:22.606
One of it is how divided
we are politically.

00:25:22.606 --> 00:25:24.526
But at the end of the
day we are the future.

00:25:24.526 --> 00:25:25.500
- That is true.

00:25:25.500 --> 00:25:28.470
- I hope that we don't
follow what they're doing.

00:25:28.470 --> 00:25:31.770
I hope that when our
generation goes into Congress,

00:25:31.770 --> 00:25:33.870
I hope that we're not
so politically divided

00:25:33.870 --> 00:25:34.703
as they are now.

00:25:34.703 --> 00:25:36.330
- One thing that gives me a lot of hope

00:25:36.330 --> 00:25:39.180
is just like all of us
right now here talking,

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:40.470
we're all from different backgrounds.

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:42.810
We've all had different
stories in our past,

00:25:42.810 --> 00:25:45.450
but we're all here and we're
all having a conversation

00:25:45.450 --> 00:25:46.950
and we're all listening to each other.

00:25:46.950 --> 00:25:49.470
We're all getting our ideas
out. And in the end of the day,

00:25:49.470 --> 00:25:51.570
I think this is giving
me hope for the future

00:25:51.570 --> 00:25:53.217
cuz this is what's gonna change.

00:25:53.217 --> 00:25:54.050
(dramatic music)

00:25:54.050 --> 00:25:55.590
- [Interviewer] Most of my friends have

00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:58.300
the same political beliefs as I do.

00:25:59.698 --> 00:26:02.031
(footsteps)

00:26:05.837 --> 00:26:10.500
- I came from a very
conservative and republican city

00:26:10.500 --> 00:26:13.470
and state in Arkansas and
I grew up around a lot

00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:15.720
of people who did not have
the same beliefs as me at all.

00:26:15.720 --> 00:26:17.850
And a lot of the people
that I would try to keep

00:26:17.850 --> 00:26:19.835
in my circle who did
have different beliefs

00:26:19.835 --> 00:26:23.520
were blasting me on private
stories and stuff like that

00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:25.956
and making me feel like I was dumb.

00:26:25.956 --> 00:26:28.380
- It's really hard for me to make friends

00:26:28.380 --> 00:26:31.980
that are from the liberal
side as immediately they hear

00:26:31.980 --> 00:26:36.210
or even see my political
views or even my religion,

00:26:36.210 --> 00:26:37.920
they immediately try to shut me down.

00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:39.150
They send me death threats.

00:26:39.150 --> 00:26:41.760
They put stuff in my bag
saying they're gonna kill me.

00:26:41.760 --> 00:26:44.520
They've poured paint in
my bag and shaken it up.

00:26:44.520 --> 00:26:47.880
When COVID happened and things
were starting to shut down

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:50.809
and the incident with
George Floyd happened,

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:53.580
everybody started looking
through everyone's profiles,

00:26:53.580 --> 00:26:54.570
their family's profiles,

00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:56.760
especially when these
protests were going on.

00:26:56.760 --> 00:26:59.580
And there was a picture
of my dad and my family,

00:26:59.580 --> 00:27:01.830
all of us together, and he
was wearing a Trump shirt.

00:27:01.830 --> 00:27:03.690
I was getting a lot of death threats,

00:27:03.690 --> 00:27:06.868
a lot of encouraging me to commit suicide,

00:27:06.868 --> 00:27:10.431
threatening to do unspeakable things to me

00:27:10.431 --> 00:27:14.490
and my family, threatening to
find my address and hurt them.

00:27:14.490 --> 00:27:18.420
I could in fact say almost
all of them were liberals.

00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:19.620
It's makes it really,

00:27:19.620 --> 00:27:22.530
really hard because the minute
that you're different from

00:27:22.530 --> 00:27:23.748
them, at least in my experience,

00:27:23.748 --> 00:27:25.890
they shut you down immediately.

00:27:25.890 --> 00:27:28.790
So I just kind of close
myself off and I stay friends

00:27:28.790 --> 00:27:32.580
with the people that
are going to respect me

00:27:32.580 --> 00:27:34.770
and respect my views.

00:27:34.770 --> 00:27:37.470
- When I came out publicly
as a conservative in 2018,

00:27:37.470 --> 00:27:38.850
it was probably one of the hardest years

00:27:38.850 --> 00:27:39.780
I've ever went through.

00:27:39.780 --> 00:27:41.578
At my school, having my opinions

00:27:41.578 --> 00:27:45.210
while looking like I did was a nonstarter.

00:27:45.210 --> 00:27:47.577
I received so many
obviously negative messages.

00:27:47.577 --> 00:27:49.260
They called me some terrible things,

00:27:49.260 --> 00:27:50.998
which I don't even
think I can say on here.

00:27:50.998 --> 00:27:53.490
But all the phrases that
you've heard, you know,

00:27:53.490 --> 00:27:55.110
get thrown at black conservatives simply

00:27:55.110 --> 00:27:57.300
for having their ideas
and make it look like

00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:59.940
I'm some sort of slave simply
for having my opinions.

00:27:59.940 --> 00:28:01.320
Making it seem like I can't think

00:28:01.320 --> 00:28:03.000
for myself because I am black.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:04.380
Not understanding that
they're perpetuating

00:28:04.380 --> 00:28:06.450
the exact same racism that they think

00:28:06.450 --> 00:28:09.000
they're fighting against
by calling me those words.

00:28:12.510 --> 00:28:16.500
- I'm from Thousand Oaks,
California and I've met people who

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:19.140
are like pretty hardcore conservatives.

00:28:19.140 --> 00:28:21.690
I feel like all of us,
when we, my friends,

00:28:21.690 --> 00:28:23.460
when we come and have these discussions,

00:28:23.460 --> 00:28:26.130
we all just want what's
best for this country.

00:28:26.130 --> 00:28:28.290
And of course we all have our own ideas

00:28:28.290 --> 00:28:29.730
of how to achieve that,

00:28:29.730 --> 00:28:33.209
but in the end we want
a world that's everyone

00:28:33.209 --> 00:28:35.130
can benefit from.

00:28:35.130 --> 00:28:38.160
And of course, unless you are able

00:28:38.160 --> 00:28:40.770
to discuss with other people
your different opinions

00:28:40.770 --> 00:28:43.560
with things and talk about the reasons

00:28:43.560 --> 00:28:47.730
why you believe certain ways
you can't make any progress

00:28:47.730 --> 00:28:48.739
with our country.

00:28:48.739 --> 00:28:50.790
- I strongly agree.

00:28:50.790 --> 00:28:53.400
And so personally, I'm from New Jersey,

00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:54.480
you can probably figure out,

00:28:54.480 --> 00:28:57.810
I have a predominantly
left-leaning friend group.

00:28:57.810 --> 00:29:01.080
I never really took
issue with that cuz it's,

00:29:01.080 --> 00:29:03.720
I feel like at the end
of the day you shouldn't

00:29:03.720 --> 00:29:06.570
be exclusively talking about
politics with the people

00:29:06.570 --> 00:29:07.403
you're friends with.

00:29:07.403 --> 00:29:09.420
Especially, it's concerning to me that,

00:29:09.420 --> 00:29:11.310
you know, based on recent studies,

00:29:11.310 --> 00:29:16.230
a growing plurality of Americans
simply refuse to be friends

00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:20.318
with people who are of
different political affiliations

00:29:20.318 --> 00:29:21.660
from them.

00:29:21.660 --> 00:29:25.680
That if anything, says
very concerning things

00:29:25.680 --> 00:29:26.880
about our country.

00:29:26.880 --> 00:29:30.120
Especially because you
know that this level

00:29:30.120 --> 00:29:31.980
of political polarization
that we're seeing

00:29:31.980 --> 00:29:34.650
now hasn't been matched
in American history

00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:37.797
since the Antebellum era of the Civil War.

00:29:37.797 --> 00:29:40.065
(applauding)

00:29:40.065 --> 00:29:43.565
(group talking inaudibly)

00:29:48.756 --> 00:29:51.506
(dramatic music)

